<title>INDIA: Bombay index firms first half net seen up 20.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Bombay index firms first half net seen up 20.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Top Indian firms which make up the benchmark Bombay stocks index will see a sharp slowdown in profit growth during the first half ended September 30, 1996, a Reuter poll revealed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The poll of 14 leading securities houses forecast an average 20.6 percent rise in the net profit of 30 index firms during the first half of 1996/97 (April-March) from around 40 percent a year ago.</p>
<p>Net sales growth was pegged at a modest 16.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
